# Keep internal / dev-only files out of the public deployment (2026-09-01
# security sweep). None of these are needed by the running site: the platform
# is the single built HTML plus the api/* serverless functions, and those
# functions read only lib/*.js and db/** — which are deliberately NOT listed
# here so they keep working. Everything below is source, tests, docs, mockups
# or a separate app skeleton, and only ever leaked implementation detail when
# served. (Excluding a file removes it from BOTH static serving and the
# function bundle, so nothing the runtime requires may appear here.)

# Sources and in-repo test/checks (the built HTML is committed separately and
# is what production serves — src/ is not needed at runtime).
SMP-Project-Folder/src/
SMP-Project-Folder/mockups/

# Dev tooling, snapshots, mockups, specs, brand references.
scripts/
design-mockups/
ui-versions/
specs/
.specify/
clients/

# A separate Next.js app skeleton, not part of the live platform.
smp-app/

# Documentation.
*.md
SMP-Project-Folder/*.md
.github/
